  provenance: "DDG-51 Engine Room L0: MMG standard method (Yasukawa & Yoshimura 2015),
    twin screw, twin rudder.\r\nHULL: L 141.0 m, B 17.74 m, d 6.52 m, 8717 t, x_G
    0.81 m, k_zz 35.25 m: the Blender layout (slice 3).\r\nDERIVATIVES: DTMB 5415
    bare hull, IIHR PMM (Yoon 2009, Iowa PhD thesis, Tables 6-2/6-3) at Fn 0.138
    / 0.280 / 0.410, interpolated by speed.\r\n  N'r at Fn 0.28/0.41 from Table 6-12
    (Table 6-3 repeats Y'r there, a typo). Cross terms Fn 0.28 IIHR (low confidence,
    12-152 % facility scatter).\r\n  Y'r: published -0.0485 makes the bare hull directionally
    unstable and turns at a third of Barry's diameters; read as containing the\r\n 
    centripetal mass term, so hydrodynamic Y'r = published + m' (0.1312). CALIBRATED
    choice between two readings of one table.\r\nADDED MASS: m'y 0.1111, J'z 0.0096
    (three-facility means, Yoon 2009 Tables 6-11..14). m'x = 0.04 m': AUTHORED (not
    found for 5415).\r\nRESISTANCE: ITTC 27th campaign C_T at Fn 0.10/0.28/0.41 (3.975/4.211/6.499e-3),
    ITTC-57 with k = 0.15 to full scale (S 2949 m\xB2),\r\n  C_R linear in Fn between
    points. x 1.443 appendage/condition factor: CALIBRATED so 100,000 shp (fact file,
    2 % shafting loss) makes 31 kn (AUTHORED within '30+ kn').\r\nPROPELLERS: MARIN
    4058 (SIMMAN 2008): D 6.15 m, P/D 0.87; K_T, K_Q quadratic fits of MARIN's polynomials
    over J 0-0.85: K_T 0.4084 -0.2871 -0.1596.\r\n  The real ship has 17 ft controllable-reversible-pitch
    screws (USNI 1994); at L0 the 5415 propeller at fixed pitch stands in.\r\n  w_P0
    0.031, t_P 0.095: SECONDARY (Kim 2018 'quoted', source not given). x'_P -0.431,
    y_P 4.65 m: DERIVED from the MARIN arrangement drawing.\r\n  C1 2.0, C2 1.6/1.1:
    AUTHORED (the standard method's KVLCC2 values; none for 5415).\r\n  Max 199 rpm
    = steady 31 kn; astern max 75 % of that (AUTHORED). Astern K_T = 0.5 x K0: CALIBRATED
    to stop from ahead full in about 1 min (USNI 1994).\r\n  Shaft rate 6 rpm/s:
    AUTHORED (USNI 1994: all stop to ahead flank in under 90 s; it also stands in
    for pitch reversal).\r\nRUDDERS: 2 spade rudders, 15.4 m\xB2 each (SIMMAN 2008),
    span 4.58 m (DERIVED from the MARIN drawing), aspect 1.36, f_alpha 2.31 (Fujii).\r\n 
    x'_R -0.47, y_R 4.75 m: DERIVED from the drawing. Rate 9 deg/s (5415 design value,
    SIMMAN). Max 35 deg (USNI 1994 'full rudder').\r\n  gamma_R 0.9, l'_R -0.9: CALIBRATED,
    least squares on Barry's turn diameters (500 yd at 10 kn / 35 deg, 1,000 yd at
    15 kn / 15 deg, 1,200 yd at 30 kn / 15 deg).\r\n  t_R 0.3, a_H 0.25, x'_H -0.45,
    epsilon 1.0, kappa 0.5, stall 35 deg with 70 % post-stall, centre of pressure
    4.5 m deep: AUTHORED (not found for 5415).\r\nLIMITS: 3-DOF manoeuvring (heel
    applied from the sway forces' depth); no wind, current or shallow water; 5415
    is 7 % beamier than this hull.\r\nROLL: hull sway force at half draught, rudders
    at their depth (with the sway added-mass reaction); extra lift damping 0.1 of
    critical at flank, scaling with speed (AUTHORED; the probes damp about 0.08 at
    rest, measured in PhysX).\n"
